.TH "waybar\-cffi" "5" "2026\-08\-07"
.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- cffi module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBcffi\fR module gives full control of a GTK widget to a third\-party dynamic library, to create more complex modules using different programming languages.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBcffi/<name>\fR
.PP
\fBmodule_path\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
The path to the dynamic library to load to control the widget.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables this module to consume all left over space dynamically.\&
.PP
Some additional configuration may be required depending on the cffi dynamic library being used.\&
.PP
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.SS C example:
.PP
An example module written in C can be found at https://github.\&com/Alexays/Waybar/resources/custom_modules/cffi_example/
.PP
Waybar config to enable the module:
.nf
.RS 4
"cffi/c_example": {
	"module_path": "\&.config/waybar/cffi/wb_cffi_example\&.so"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.PP
.SH DEVELOPING CFFI MODULES
.PP
CFFI modules require a handful of functions and constants to be defined with C
linkage.\& The way to achieve this depends on the programming language being used
(search for FFI / Foreign Function Interface for that language).\&
.PP
The complete list of symbols to define can be found in the header file shipped with
Waybar at \fBresources/custom_modules/cffi_example/waybar_cffi_module.\&h\fR, and a full
example written in C is provided in \fBresources/custom_modules/cffi_example/\fR.\&
.PP
Language bindings exist for several languages, including Rust (the \fBwaybar\-cffi\fR
crate) and Zig.\&
.PP
.SH STYLE
.PP
The classes and IDs are managed by the cffi dynamic library.\&
